<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 320 860" role="img" aria-labelledby="title desc">
<title id="title">Zane Wang — building tools that make AI coding agents more reliable</title>
<desc id="desc">A pixel-art sunset over a city drawn from the past 12 months of Zane's GitHub contributions. As the image loads, the contribution graph appears along the horizon and rises into the city: one building per week, taller when the week was busier, and one window per day, lit on the {{ACTIVE_DAYS}} days he contributed. A gold pennant flies over each week in which one of his pull requests was merged upstream ({{FLAG_WEEKS}} weeks, {{FLAG_PRS}} PRs). Below the city, the tools he maintains: claudemem, memory that lasts across agent sessions (about 11,000 lines of Go and nearly as many in tests); handoff, which lets a strong model delegate to cheaper ones through resumable specs, with a published evaluation; dev-orchestrator, a Claude Code plugin that takes a task to a tested pull request, failing test first. Then 12 PRs merged into 10 upstream projects ({{MERGED_RANGE}}), 10 bug fixes and 2 small features: axum, SQLx and goose in Rust; AnyIO, Tenacity and Feast in Python; Zod, TanStack Query, Fastify and Claude HUD in JavaScript and TypeScript. He uses AI to find and draft fixes, verifies each one locally, and sees it through maintainer review. His production background covers multimodal evaluation and high-volume data systems; his current public focus is tools for reliable AI coding agents.</desc>
<!-- Fonts: Departure Mono (c) Helena Zhang and IBM Plex Mono (c) IBM Corp., both SIL Open Font License 1.1; embedded as renamed subsets. -->
<!-- The phone layout of dusk.svg.template, served by the README's <picture> below 600 px: authored 320 units wide
     for a README column of about 300-350 px, on a 2-unit pixel grid. Plex Mono sizes give whole-unit
     advances (0.6 em), so lines measure the same on every platform. text-rendering:geometricPrecision keeps
     them exact when the image is scaled: Chrome otherwise rounds each advance to a whole screen pixel.
     Type: 11 pixel labels, 11.67 notes (7-unit advance), 13.33 tagline and names (8), 44 name. The same
     opening as the desktop: the contribution graph along the horizon rises into the city. The axis names
     every third month; everything under it is one column. -->
<defs><style>{{FONT_FACES}}
text{text-rendering:geometricPrecision}
.px{font-family:zw-pixel, ui-monospace, 'SF Mono', Menlo, Consolas, 'DejaVu Sans Mono', monospace}
.bd{font-family:zw-body, ui-monospace, 'SF Mono', Menlo, Consolas, 'DejaVu Sans Mono', monospace}
.md{font-family:zw-body-medium, ui-monospace, 'SF Mono', Menlo, Consolas, 'DejaVu Sans Mono', monospace}
.b{transform-box:fill-box;transform-origin:50% 100%;animation:rise 1.4s cubic-bezier(.65,0,.35,1) both}@keyframes rise{from{transform:scaleY(0)}to{transform:scaleY(1)}}
.m{transform-box:fill-box;transform-origin:0 0;animation-duration:1.4s;animation-timing-function:cubic-bezier(.65,0,.35,1);animation-fill-mode:both}
@keyframes mv{from{transform:var(--t)}to{transform:none}}
.c0{animation-name:mv,c0}.c1{animation-name:mv,c1}.c2{animation-name:mv,c2}.c3{animation-name:mv,c3}.c4{animation-name:mv,c4}
@keyframes c0{0%{fill:#161b22}100%{fill:#3d2c38}}@keyframes c1{0%{fill:#0e4429}100%{fill:#f6db95}}@keyframes c2{0%{fill:#006d32}100%{fill:#f6db95}}
@keyframes c3{0%{fill:#26a641}100%{fill:#f6db95}}@keyframes c4{0%{fill:#39d353}100%{fill:#f6db95}}
.tw{animation:tw 3.4s ease-in-out infinite}@keyframes tw{0%,100%{opacity:.2}50%{opacity:.95}}
.glow{animation:glow 7s ease-in-out infinite}@keyframes glow{0%,100%{opacity:.75}50%{opacity:1}}
.sh{animation:sh 2.8s ease-in-out infinite}@keyframes sh{0%,100%{opacity:.25}50%{opacity:.9}}
.beacon{animation:bk 1.6s steps(1) infinite}@keyframes bk{0%{opacity:1}50%{opacity:.15}}
@media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){*{animation:none!important}}</style>
